88. Loneliness (UCLS)-[POSITIVE]->Perceived stress (PSS)
   Properties: {'original_motivation': "Loneliness (UCLS) causes Perceived stress (PSS) through a direct causal mechanism. Increased loneliness can heighten an individual's perception of stress due to reduced social support and greater emotional burden. Conversely, lower loneliness leads to lower perceived stress. This direct, positive relationship is supported by established psychological theories and is not fully mediated by other variables in the provided CLD.", 'session_id': '00f0553c-397a-4306-abda-8c7c4b448985', 'prob_std': 0.3175187426883103, 'citations': ['https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30825769/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0167494319300433', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3874845/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9910279/'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7161293055312706, 'is_corrupted': True, 'motivation': 'Loneliness (UCLS) causes Perceived stress (PSS) because individuals experiencing higher levels of loneliness tend to have fewer daily tasks and social obligations, leading to more unstructured time. This abundance of free time allows for excessive rumination on minor inconveniences, which amplifies stress perceptions. Therefore, as Loneliness (UCLS) increases, the lack of distraction from social engagements directly increases Perceived stress (PSS), irrespective of social support or emotional factors.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'spurious_motivation': 'Loneliness (UCLS) causes Perceived stress (PSS) because individuals experiencing higher levels of loneliness tend to have fewer daily tasks and social obligations, leading to more unstructured time. This abundance of free time allows for excessive rumination on minor inconveniences, which amplifies stress perceptions. Therefore, as Loneliness (UCLS) increases, the lack of distraction from social engagements directly increases Perceived stress (PSS), irrespective of social support or emotional factors.', 'perplexity': 1.6341963727581665, 'mean_to